# Add "Move to Workspace" context menu option

## Context

Agents are assigned a workspace at spawn time but cannot be reassigned afterward. The agent sidebar context menu needs a "Move to…" option that lets users move an agent to a different workspace (or unassign it).

## Changes

### 1. Add message type — `lib/types.ts`

Add `BrowserMoveAgent` interface and include it in the `BrowserMessage` union:

```ts
export interface BrowserMoveAgent {
  type: "move_agent";
  agentId: string;
  workspaceId: string | null;
}
```

### 2. Add server handler — `server/ws.ts`

Add a `case "move_agent"` handler following the same pattern as `pin_agent`/`icebox_agent`:

```ts
case "move_agent": {
  const agent = agents.get(msg.agentId);
  if (!agent) break;
  agent.workspaceId = msg.workspaceId;
  broadcastAgentList();
  persistAgentSync(agent);
  break;
}
```

### 3. Add hook action — `hooks/use-websocket.ts`

Add a `moveAgent` callback following the `iceboxAgent` pattern:

```ts
const moveAgent = useCallback(
  (agentId: string, workspaceId: string | null) => {
    send({ type: "move_agent", agentId, workspaceId });
  },
  [send]
);
```

Return it from the hook.

### 4. Wire through dashboard — `app/dashboard/page.tsx`

Pass `moveAgent` to `<AgentSidebar>` as `onMoveAgent`.

### 5. Add submenu to context menu — `components/dashboard/agent-sidebar.tsx`

- Add `onMoveAgent` prop to `AgentSidebar`
- Add a "Move to…" item in the context menu (between Icebox and Rename) that expands a submenu on hover showing:
  - Each workspace (excluding the agent's current workspace)
  - "No workspace" option if the agent currently has one
- On selection: call `onMoveAgent(agentId, workspaceId)` and close the menu
- Submenu uses the same styling as the parent menu, positioned to the right

## Files modified

1. `lib/types.ts` — new `BrowserMoveAgent` interface + union member
2. `server/ws.ts` — `move_agent` case handler
3. `hooks/use-websocket.ts` — `moveAgent` callback + return value
4. `app/dashboard/page.tsx` — pass `onMoveAgent={moveAgent}` to sidebar
5. `components/dashboard/agent-sidebar.tsx` — new prop + submenu UI

## Verification

1. `pnpm build` — confirm no type errors
2. `pnpm dev` — open dashboard, right-click an agent, hover "Move to…", verify workspace list appears, select a workspace, confirm agent moves (disappears from current workspace view if scoped)

